---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Contribute" description="How to add a device capture to the tutti corpus.">
  <header>
    <p class="page-eyebrow">For contributors</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Add a device</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      tutti runs on your LAN, captures what it sees, and writes a paste-ready
      bundle to disk. Submitting a capture is a single MR.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2 class="section-title">1. Run tutti against your LAN</h2>
    <pre class="code-block">
# Build from source (binaries land with v0.1.0).
git clone https://gitlab.com/dunn.dev/tutti.git
cd tutti
make build

# Capture the LAN. Drive runs are opt-in via --drive; tutti refuses
# to interrupt a device that's currently in PLAYING state unless you
# also pass --force.
./tutti capture --drive --contributor github:your-handle</pre>
    <p class="section-prose">
      Output lands in <code>./capture-&lt;timestamp&gt;-&lt;host&gt;/</code>. Open
      the directory and review what tutti wrote: SSDP/mDNS dumps, the
      device descriptor, GetProtocolInfo sink list, and per-tone drive
      transcripts. Edit <code>notes.md</code> if there's context worth adding
      ("the device is slow to wake," "I had to disable IPv6," etc.).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="section-title">2. Validate locally</h2>
    <pre class="code-block">make validate DIR=./capture-&lt;timestamp&gt;-&lt;host&gt;</pre>
    <p class="section-prose">
      The same validator runs in CI. If it fails locally, the failure
      message tells you the next action — schema-shape, vacuity rule,
      or redaction-not-recorded. CI will reject the MR with the same
      message.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="section-title">3. Submit as a merge request</h2>
    <p class="section-prose">
      Move the capture into the corpus tree:
    </p>
    <pre class="code-block">mkdir -p evidence/&lt;vendor&gt;-&lt;model&gt;/captures/
mv ./capture-&lt;ts&gt;-&lt;host&gt; evidence/&lt;vendor&gt;-&lt;model&gt;/captures/&lt;ts&gt;-&lt;contributor&gt;
# Open an MR on https://gitlab.com/dunn.dev/tutti</pre>
    <p class="section-prose">
      The site rebuilds on merge. Your capture appears in the device
      list and gets its own page within minutes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="section-title">What's preserved, what's redacted</h2>
    <p class="section-prose">
      tutti scrubs RFC1918 LAN addresses, Subsonic auth params (user,
      token, salt), and Authorization headers from every transcript by
      default. The manifest records every redaction it applied, so a
      reader of the bundle always knows what was stripped.
    </p>
    <p class="section-prose">
      The device's UDN is preserved on purpose: it's central to bug
      evidence, advertised on every multicast, and not sensitive in
      isolation.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .code-block {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: var(--space-3) 0;
  }
  .section-title {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: var(--space-7) 0 var(--space-3) 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .section-prose {
    color: var(--text-2);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
</style>
